        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allouez_Township%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew around a mine and a station on the Hancock & Calumet Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allouez_Township%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Allouez’s name honors the Ojibwe, an Anishinaabe Native American group indigenous to the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allouez_Township%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Keweenaw National Historical Park, though not fully inside Allouez, is easily accessible and showcases the region’s copper mining history.",
